\id PHM Original Douay-Rheims (1582/1610)
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h Philemon
\toc1 The Epistle of Paul to Philemon.
\toc2 Philemon
\toc3 PHM
\mt1 The Epistle of Paul to Philemon.
\c 1
\cd Hearing of Philémons vertue, vvho vvas a Coloſſian, he vvriteth a familiar letter from Rome (being priſoner there) about his fugitiue ſeruant Oneſimus: not doubting but that he might commaund him, yet rather requeſting that he vvil forgiue him, yea and receiue him as he vvould Paul him ſelf, who alſo hopeth to come vnto him.
\p
\v 1 \sc PAVL\sc* the priſoner of Chriſt \sc IESVS\sc*, and brother Timothee: to Philémon the beloued and our coadiutor,
\v 2 & to Appia our deereſt ſiſter, & to Archippus our felovv-ſouldiar and to the church vvhich is in thy houſe.
\v 3 Grace to you and peace from God our father, and our Lord \sc IESVS\sc* Chriſt.
\v 4 I giue thankes to my God, alvvaies making a memorie of thee in my praiers,
\v 5 hearing thy \f 1 \fr 1.5 \ft Faith and charitie commended alwais together, both neceſſarie to make a complete Chriſtian man, and to iuſtification & ſaluation.\f* charitie and faith vvhich thou haſt in our Lord \sc IESVS\sc*, and tovvard al the ſainctes: \ef - \fr 1.5 \fq Tovvard al the ſainctes. \ft ¹ The Apoſtle ſticketh not to ſay, Charitie and faith in Chriſt and al his Saincts, vvhich our captious Aduerſaries count in Catholike mens ſpeaches and writings, very abſurd, feining that in al ſuch vve make no difference betvvixt the loue vve beare to Chriſt, and the loue vve owe to our neighbours: betvvixt the truſt or beleefe vve haue in God, and that which we haue in his holy Saincts. Malice and contention doth ſo blinde al Heretikes. \fq ¹ \ft Faith and beleefe in Saincts.\ef*
\v 6 that the communication of thy faith may be made euident in the agnition of al \f 1 \fr 1.6 \ft \+it * good work\+it*\f* good that is in you in Chriſt \sc IESVS\sc*.
\v 7 For I haue had great ioy and conſolation in thy charitie, becauſe the bovvels of the ſainctes \f 1 \fr 1.7 \ft The dueties of charitie and mercie done to Chriſtes priſoners, are exceding acceptable to God and al good men.\f* haue reſted by thee brother.
\v 8 For the vvhich thing hauing great confidence in Chriſt \sc IESVS\sc* to commaund thee that vvhich pertaineth to the purpoſe:
\v 9 for charitie rather I beſeeche, vvhereas thou art ſuch an one, as Paul being old and novv priſoner alſo of \sc IESVS\sc* Chriſt.
\v 10 I beſeeche thee for my ſonne vvhom I haue begotten in bandes, \x - \xt Col. 4, 9.\x* Oneſimus,
\v 11 vvho hath been ſometime vnprofitable to thee, but novv profitable both to me & thee,
\v 12 vvhom I haue ſent backe to thee. And \f 1 \fr 1.12 \ft Al Spiritual men ought to be exceding propenſe and ready to procure mens pardon, and reconciliation to al penitents.\f* do thou receiue him as mine ovvne bovvels.
\v 13 vvhom I would haue reteined vvith me, that for thee he might miniſter to me in the bandes of the Goſpel:
\v 14 but vvithout thy counſel I vvould doe nothing: that thy good might be not as it vvere of neceſſitie, but voluntarie.
\v 15 For perhaps therfore he departed for a ſeaſon from thee, that thou mighteſt take him againe for euer.
\v 16 novv not as a ſeruant, but for a ſeruant, a moſt deere brother, eſpecially to me, but hovv much more to thee both in the fleſh and in our Lord?
\v 17 If therfore thou take me for thy fellovv: receiue him as my ſelf.
\v 18 And if he hath hurt thee any thing or is in thy dette, that impute to me.
\v 19 I Paul haue vvritten vvith mine ovvne hand: I vvil repay it: not to ſay to thee, \f 1 \fr 1.19 \ft The great debt & duetie that vve owe to ſuch as be our ſpiritual parents in Chriſt.\f* that thou ovveſt me thine ovvne ſelf alſo.
\v 20 Yea brother. \f 1 \fr 1.20 \ft \+it c ὀναίμησ\+it*\f* God graunt I may enioy thee in our Lord. Refreſh my bovvels in our Lord.
\v 21 Truſting in thy obedience I haue vvritten to thee, knovving that thou vvilt doe aboue that alſo vvhich I do ſay.
\v 22 And withal prouide me alſo a lodging. for I hope by your praiers that I ſhal be giuen to you.
\v 23 There ſalute thee Epaphras my fellovv-priſoner in Chriſt \sc IESVS\sc*,
\v 24 Marke, Ariſtarchus, Demas and Luke my coadiutors.
\v 25 The grace of our Lord \sc IESVS\sc* Chriſt be with your ſpirit. Amen,
